                                        "sense_id": "dfca4cc1-b8ad-3950-8f3d-a6c3608f982b",
                                        "entry_id": "89aec7c6-f805-3f5a-ab50-bb87dcb9491d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an audio signal: having a thin sound as a result of connection through only one wire of a circuit pair."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2dde879b-e1e0-459c-a61c-367a162aea18",
                                                "sense_id": "dfca4cc1-b8ad-3950-8f3d-a6c3608f982b",
                                                "text": "[…] obviously wrong termination is likely to lead to a thin 'one-legged' sound with significant loss of level, and/or distortion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e747b0b-5d3f-4069-9182-77e82892c0e7",
                                                "sense_id": "dfca4cc1-b8ad-3950-8f3d-a6c3608f982b",
                                                "text": "[…] you have to bear in mind that your sound files in these circumstances will have a one legged stereo recording."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "one-legged",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb123795-0b34-32db-bce3-4b22d0dea653",
                                        "entry_id": "9112338f-fa6d-35a6-9455-0fe94aba59d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant, especially a tree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54b988fe-fd80-4b09-967d-134f02e1a07c",
                                                "sense_id": "cb123795-0b34-32db-bce3-4b22d0dea653",
                                                "text": "In other words, people engage in communicative relationships not only with other people, but also with four-leggeds, one-leggeds, and no-leggeds, with trees, plants, and rocks, with the sun, moon, and stars, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37ba5142-3405-4a33-8a3f-d48952196ea0",
                                                "sense_id": "cb123795-0b34-32db-bce3-4b22d0dea653",
                                                "text": "We were talking about how Catolicos seemed to not see the one-leggeds and four-leggeds as sacred."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fa568d3-0d2d-4cc4-971f-bbdf66a8a51a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb123795-0b34-32db-bce3-4b22d0dea653",
                                                "text": "The arrow, for instance, combines gifts of stone for the head (from no-leggeds, who live within the Earth), wood for the shaft (from one-leggeds, trees, who unite Earth and Sky, and resembling the bole), and feathers (from two-leggeds, who live in the Sky); the stone is its head (Thoreau called arrowheads \"fossilized thoughts\"), the shaft its body, the feathers its wings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
